Need to compute next occurrence epoch. Convention: 
```c
static int64_t cron_next_daily_epoch(uint8_t hour, uint8_t minute, time_t now)
{
    const int tz_offset = 8 * 3600; /* AGENT_TIMEZONE "CST-8" => UTC+8 */
    time_t local_now = now + tz_offset;
    struct tm local_tm;
    gmtime_r(&local_now, &local_tm);

    /* Seconds since local midnight now */
    int now_sec = local_tm.tm_hour * 3600 + local_tm.tm_min * 60 + local_tm.tm_sec;
    int target_sec = (int)hour * 3600 + (int)minute * 60;
    int delta = target_sec - now_sec;
    if (delta <= 0) {
        delta += 86400;
    }

    return (int64_t)(now + delta);
}
```
This returns UTC epoch (now is UTC epoch; delta computed in local wall-clock terms, and DST isn't a concern for CST). Good. Document the offset assumption.

